        "Text": {
          "type": "cexolocstring",
          "value": {
            "0": "*A stout, silver-whiskered hobbit looks up from a great unrolled scroll of names, quill behind his ear.* Ah -- a fresh pair of eyes! Odo Proudfoot, at your service, and keeper of the Hobbiton family-books. There is a dispute afoot, you see: the Ivy Bush is fair split over who is cousin to whom, and the argument shifts with every season like the wind off the Hill. I'll put five questions of Shire lineage to you -- answer four rightly and I'll count you a friend of the family-books and see you rewarded. Will you match wits with an old genealogist?"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "__struct_id": 1,
        "Animation": {
          "type": "dword",
          "value": 0
        },
        "AnimLoop": {
          "type": "byte",
